 [17592186073053 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "801c153b-8efc-5afa-ac4a-b73e0e4da6c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073054 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073054 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073054 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bf815c02-91cb-598c-a95a-f67c4a74fc21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073055 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073055 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073055 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c2d533c1-1a07-519e-814a-583ef7b450de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073056 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073056 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073056 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dbfc7cee-81a8-50d2-abb0-e16d24fedcc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073057 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073057 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073057 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6524afed-5762-5779-9618-c752a0358bfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073587 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2647" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073587 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the distance between the points $(2,4)$ and $(5,4)$?\n\n![](images/ce/ce70a8122559f67aac379349fb369e6e7e007e85fa8a13632e7865469804fb6a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073587 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fb5d2269-5350-5d79-9414-1a25caa48d8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073587 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $3$ units, so the distance equals $3$.\n\n![](images/bd/bd568e789e79574225dbd75e79d4cacb2fbf92beb048f5bdafeb67f74ab029f6.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/fb/fb2f075f8321aca3823770e28a86a8d9532cb343ba4239f94c2fb9d1cc883b0b.png)\n\nThe point $({\\color{blue}{5}},4)$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{5}$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $({\\color{red}{2}},4)$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{2}$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{5}} - {\\color{red}{2}} = 3\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073588 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2648" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073588 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the distance between the points $(-4,-2)$ and $(-4,-5)$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073588 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1250785a-1ae3-5218-925a-0eac01281f3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073588 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/0d/0d26dd64fad1809f58fecdf802a28b5ab6d1dd201b63dc0bb9293f248a127a85.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $3$ units, so the distance equals $3$.\n\n![](images/fb/fbc52312edf77508a9d7436acd515bc91e3225826c16b85c3571143c39886771.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/80/80be7ec0ed67ce819b51b34f7a50aeb51786e3a6ca9190b418b2ec96e127cc78.png)\n\nThe point $(-4,{\\color{red}{-5}})$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{5}$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(-4,{\\color{blue}{-2}})$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{2}$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{5}} - {\\color{blue}{2}} = 3\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073589 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073589 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the distance between the points $(3,4)$ and $(3,-3)$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073589 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e05457af-60c5-519f-935e-db465fc76efa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073589 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/47/47f203755bf0abcbf33be636331e4f9c0119c14620f1a658be31db0d6feeed17.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $7$ units, so the distance equals $7$.\n\n![](images/79/79b944cc0d1af7577282653e3250af844ad10256bb3b6cf2b204ed2f9862d480.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/94/94a5e438b160ce6f3dca0f44fd418a8831c520543e7dad605ea23674500af5fd.png)\n\nThe point $(3,{\\color{blue}{4}})$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{4}$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(3,{\\color{red}{-3}})$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{3}$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{3}} + {\\color{blue}{4}} = 7\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073898 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073898 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073898 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073898 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073898 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Horizontal Distance Between Two Points" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073898 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073898 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1d9b6948-92f4-58b3-8c06-fae61765dc57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073899 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073899 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073899 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Vertical Distance Between Two Points" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073899 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073899 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f0708cd3-0608-5d57-ac14-4c16ef362473" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073900 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074468 #edb/re